$input_json — load a bundle manifest from JSON

SUMMARY
  Reads an output.json- or input.json-shaped manifest and rebuilds an
  ArrayBundle so a pipeline can continue from a previous session step or
  reuse assets without re-running upstream work.

SYNTAX
  $input_json('sessions/20260519_051548_2592/11__music/output.json')
  $input_json('path/to/output.json', strict=1)

INPUT
  Ignored — the JSON file is the sole data source for this step.

OUTPUT
  All arrays present in the JSON: prompts, texts, images, sounds, videos,
  files, changes (same keys as session output.json).

ARGUMENTS
  Positional path or path= / _path= — path to the JSON manifest.
  strict=1 | true | yes — fail if any linked file on disk is missing.

BEHAVIOR
  Resolves the JSON path relative to the launch folder, current session dir,
  or cwd. Relative links in the manifest resolve under the launch folder;
  $output exports (output/<session_id>/...) always map to
  <launch-dir>/output/<session_id>/ regardless of session-relative prefixes.

EXAMPLE
  @restore: $input_json('sessions/…/11__music/output.json')
  @test_clip: $input_json('…/12__image_clip/input.json') -> $image_clip

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
